---
/**
 * Jude's Playlist — gloriouslyunhinged.com/judes-playlist
 *
 * ⚠️ This URL is printed in the book as a QR code.
 *    NEVER rename or delete this file after the book is printed.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Paste the playlist ID here: the part after "list=" in the playlist URL.
const playlistId = 'PLfq7qtYoG7Sk';

const embedUrl = `https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/videoseries?list=${playlistId}`;
const youtubeMusicUrl = `https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=${playlistId}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Jude's Playlist — Blurred Borders — Gloriously Unhinged"
  description="Jude's curated list of whatever the fuck he felt like at the time. The official Blurred Borders playlist."
  image="/bbcoverpulp5.png"
>
  <header class="page-header centered">
    <p class="kicker">Blurred Borders</p>
    <h1>Jude's Playlist</h1>
    <p class="page-subtitle">
      Curated with all the care and precision of a man in a maid uniform
      who should have been doing surveillance.
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="page-section prose">
    <p>
      You scanned a QR code in a dark romance novel. Look at you.
      Thriving.
    </p>
    <p>
      These are the songs Jude picked. There was no system. There was no theme.
      There was a federal agency that should have known better, a household he
      was supposed to be investigating, an apron, and a man choosing
      <em>whatever the fuck he felt like at the time.</em> We respect him far
      too much to impose order on it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Press play. Do the dishes. Question your choices. It worked for him.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section">
    <div class="player">
      <iframe
        src={embedUrl}
        title="Jude's Playlist"
        allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share"
        referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
        allowfullscreen
        loading="lazy"
      ></iframe>
    </div>

    <p class="player-note">
      YouTube may sneak ads in between songs. We don't control those.
      Rafi has been informed and is looking into it.
    </p>

    <div class="player-links">
      <a href={youtubeMusicUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-outline">
        Open in YouTube Music
      </a>
      <a href="/books" class="btn btn-outline">
        About Blurred Borders
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .kicker {
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.3em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .page-subtitle {
    max-width: 480px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

    /* Square 250x250 music player, centered */
  .player {
    box-sizing: content-box;
    width: 300px;
    height: 300px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    position: relative;
    border: 1px solid var(--surface-border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--surface);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
  }

  .player iframe {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border: 0;
  }

  .player-note {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-style: italic;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
  }

  .player-links {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }
</style>